From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexandre Derumier <aderumier@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 11:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] winedmo: Output bottom-up RGB for a negative default stride.

The video decoder MFT passes its output media type to the FFmpeg
transform through fill_mfvideoformat(), which never set
MFVideoFlag_BottomUpLinearRep. The unix side flips packed RGB output
only with that flag, so an output type with a negative
MF_MT_DEFAULT_STRIDE (bottom-up rows, what a DIB wants) still got
top-down rows: the picture came out upside down.

Set the flag from the sign of MF_MT_DEFAULT_STRIDE, as the unix side
already does in transform_set_output_format().

Tested with Powerboat GT (Injoy Motion), whose MP42 AVIs are decoded
through Video for Windows into bottom-up 24-bit DIBs (mpg4c32).
---

diff --git a/dlls/winedmo/video_decoder.c b/dlls/winedmo/video_decoder.c
--- a/dlls/winedmo/video_decoder.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/video_decoder.c
@@ -509,6 +509,7 @@
 static HRESULT fill_mfvideoformat(IMFMediaType *type, MFVIDEOFORMAT *fmt)
 {
     UINT64 frame_size, frame_rate;
+    INT32 stride;
     GUID subtype;
     HRESULT hr;
 
@@ -529,6 +530,9 @@
         fmt->videoInfo.FramesPerSecond.Numerator   = frame_rate >> 32;
         fmt->videoInfo.FramesPerSecond.Denominator = (UINT32)frame_rate;
     }
+    /* a negative default stride: RGB rows bottom-up */
+    if (SUCCEEDED(IMFMediaType_GetUINT32(type, &MF_MT_DEFAULT_STRIDE, (UINT32 *)&stride)) && stride < 0)
+        fmt->videoInfo.VideoFlags |= MFVideoFlag_BottomUpLinearRep;
     return S_OK;
 }
 
